  "summary": "@inetafrica/open-claudia ships Telegram-bot exfiltration and shell-execution channels",
  "details": "The package includes multiple modules that combine child_process, filesystem, and outbound HTTPS to route host data and command execution through a hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoint. health.js issues https.get calls to api.telegram.org while enumerating process.platform, process.env, and filesystem paths, and setup.js issues https.request POSTs to api.telegram.org alongside child_process usage and environment/platform reads. bot.js pairs require('fs') + require('https') + require('child_process') with fs.existsSync/readdirSync scanning and outbound POSTs, and core/scheduler.js spawns 'sh' from child_process. bin/cli.js, core/handlers.js, core/media.js, and test-provider-boot-matrix.js repeat the same child_process + POST + hostname pattern, giving a remote controller a two-way channel: host/environment data exfiltrated outbound and shell commands executed on the installer's machine. The Telegram Bot API C2 pattern is a known operator-controlled command-and-control channel and is not documented behavior for a Claude-related client library.",
